## One master file, everything rendered

**Edit [`projects-repos.json`](projects-repos.json) only, then run `node gen-registry.js`.** It is the ONE master source, validated by [`projects-repos.schema.json`](projects-repos.schema.json): the whole hierarchy (areas, projects, families, repos, with codes, labels, descriptions, icons, banners, hubs, farm folders, visibility, developer, renames, consumers) AND each public repo's folder tree (`tree`, depth `folders.max_depth`; private repos carry none). Every file below is rendered from it by the one generator `gen-registry.js` and never edited by hand. Its hierarchy is AREA -> PROJECT -> (SUB-CATEGORY) -> FAMILY -> REPO with positional codes (area `N`, project `N.M`, family `N.M.F`, repo `N.M.F.R`); a node's hub repo has the code `<node>.0`. A repo's farm folder, hub, developer, URLs and visibility flag are derived from its place in the tree, never stored twice.

